            <ArticleTitle>Progression of the milking effect of the coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>475-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial bridging and systolic milking may be involved in myocardial ischemia, myocardial infarction, and sudden death. We describe a patient whose milking effect progressed significantly over a two-year period. We conclude that bridging and milking effect can progress over a relatively short period. In those patients with prior reports of insignificant bridging and milking on coronary arteriograms and continued angina-like chest pain, a repeated catheterization may be warranted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
